Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:01:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] window: the Apex disk footer and item-count bar

The Apex Files window (src/apex/, Source1) adds two widgets, both from
apex_window_attach() in nautilus_window_init(), once the template is
built:

- the disk footer under the places sidebar: the free space and size of
  the filesystem holding the home folder, with a meter;
- the item-count bar at the bottom of the content: the items of the
  active view, or the results while searching, and the selection.

With APEX_NAUTILUS_STOCK=1 it does nothing.
---
 src/nautilus-window.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nautilus-window.c b/src/nautilus-window.c
index 4ca67af..1b26507 100644
--- a/src/nautilus-window.c
+++ b/src/nautilus-window.c
@@ -69,6 +69,8 @@
 #include "nautilus-ui-utilities.h"
 #include "nautilus-window-slot.h"
 
+#include "apex/apex-window.h"
+
 static void nautilus_window_initialize_actions (NautilusWindow *window);
 static void nautilus_window_sync_location_widgets (NautilusWindow *window);
 static void update_cursor (NautilusWindow *window);
@@ -1571,6 +1573,8 @@ nautilus_window_init (NautilusWindow *window)
     window->active_slot = NULL;
 
     gtk_widget_add_css_class (GTK_WIDGET (window), "nautilus-window");
+    apex_window_attach (ADW_APPLICATION_WINDOW (window), GTK_WIDGET (window->places_sidebar),
+                        GTK_WIDGET (window->tab_view));
 
     window_group = gtk_window_group_new ();
     gtk_window_group_add_window (window_group, GTK_WINDOW (window));
